        <maml:para>Retrieves detailed execution history for SSIS packages from the SSIS catalog database, including execution status, timing, and environment details. This command queries the catalog.executions view in SSISDB to provide comprehensive execution information for troubleshooting failed packages, monitoring performance, and analyzing SSIS workloads.</maml:para>
        <maml:para>Useful for identifying failed or long-running packages, tracking execution patterns over time, and investigating SSIS deployment issues. Results can be filtered by project, folder, environment, execution status, or date range to focus on specific troubleshooting scenarios.</maml:para>
      </maml:description>
